            <ArticleTitle>Dilated cardiomyopathy with recurrent intraventricular thrombosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>487-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dilated cardiomyopathy with intraventricular thrombosis is a rare disease, most frequently encountered in adults. It rarely occurs in infants. We report here the case of a 2-year-old boy with intraventricular thrombosis due to dilated cardiomyopathy and emphasize the importance of prophylactic anticoagulant therapy in this case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
